This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: The amulet of Yendor should slowly increase in weight after you
first pick it up, kind of like the one ring did for Frodo. Should make
Astral a bit more challenging. --scwizard

[2]: Applying the Scepter of Might to a rock enchants it. Only for
caveman of course. --SpeedEvil

[3]: Hitting a water elemental (or perhaps other water based creatures
like ;) with a cold attack or with Frost Brand should cause the monster
to become temporarily immobile/paralyzed. --Jmadman311

[4]: Cursed tins come with a chance of creating a stinking cloud when
opened. --lament

[5]: <a>pplying $ should allow you to toss a coin, giving a heads/tails
message. --Wolfechu

[6]: (A)pplying a camera should light up a room/radius temporarily.
--ekiM

[7]: "Auto-open" option. Attempt to open doors when walking into them.
--Dentarthurdent_

[8]: If you die by choking on an artifact weapon, you should get
"choked on Magicbane" instead of "choked on a Magicbane".
--Dentarthurdent_

[9]: when polymorphed into a flying monster, you ought to be able to
reach the bottom of a pit. --Dentarthurdent_

[10]: if your character is too wimpy (say, < XL 5), summoned demons
instakill him. "Blood covers the altar! You have summoned Yeenoghu! He
bites your head off!" --lament

[11]: Leprechauns should be dangerous to gold golems, like rusting is
to iron golems. --NESoutlaw_

[12]: how about some nice artifact BoH, [HoB, "oR, [GoP, robe, or
indeed anything suitable for a weaponless monk? I am sick of saccing a
lot then getting yet another longsword. --SimonRC

[13]: monsters should flee if they see a large number of their species'
corpses --shel-

[14]: You should be able to bless/curse things on the ground by pouring
(un)holy water on them. --Dentarthurdent_

[15]: an apron should reduce/nullify damage received by acid/water
explosions. --braindancer

[16]: MUMAKROTTA --lament


